NEMS Open
Copyright 2026 Josh Agarwal and contributors

This project ports the U.S. Energy Information Administration's National
Energy Modeling System (NEMS, github.com/EIAgov/NEMS) to Python, and tests
it against EIA's published AEO2026 reference case.

Source: U.S. Energy Information Administration, National Energy Modeling
System, AEO2026 release (2026).

NEMS is a U.S. government work; EIA states that U.S. government publications
are in the public domain, and releases its other open-source models under
Apache 2.0. This project is not affiliated with or endorsed by EIA. No EIA
source code is included in this repository; the oracle build fetches EIA's
code from EIA's own repository and patches a local copy.

EIA data in this repository: web/data/ holds numbers taken from or computed
from EIA's published AEO2026 runs (the reference series shown as "EIA
reference", and results of this project's models fitted to those runs), and
web/data/engine.json holds line counts and routine names read from EIA's
source. src/nems_open/supply_standin/coefficients.json and
src/nems_open/demand_elasticities.json are fitted to EIA's runs.
